## Implemented Contract

- Consumes the authoritative P7-00 `GridDrawPacket`, `GridLinePacket`, and
  `GizmoDrawPacket` together with frozen `EditorViewportMetrics`; it does not
  adapt the older public `EditorOverlayFrame` contract.
- Uses only logical RHI handles. It owns an immutable 4,116-vertex / 20,124-index
  canonical Gizmo atlas, a scene-depth sampler, frame-local uniform/line
  buffers and argument tables, helper depth, shader library, and eight fixed
  pipeline variants.
- Declares output as read-write `ColorAttachment` at `rasterColorOut`, scene
  depth as fragment `ShaderRead`, and helper depth as write
  `DepthStencilAttachment` at `rasterDepthOut/depthStencil`.
- Records output load/store and helper clear/store. Grid is additive and scene
  depth rejected, X/Z axes are alpha-over and always on top, and Gizmo uses
  helper self-depth with solid x-ray, optional occlusion dither, and checker
  planes. Draw order is Grid, axes, then the canonical 13 Gizmo components.
- Expands lines into triangles in shader code. Homogeneous view-volume clipping
  handles signed W plus zero-to-one and negative-one-to-one depth ranges before
  division. Logical-space normals preserve line width under nonuniform DPI and
  all D4 axis-swapping transforms.
- Maps color fragment centers through color/depth physical rectangles without
  an extra half-texel offset. Forward/reverse-Z scene comparison, helper clear,
  and helper compare derive from the same viewport convention.
- Uses explicit row vectors for row-major `OverlayMatrix4`. The frame ABI is
  160 bytes, line instance 48 bytes, Gizmo vertex 24 bytes, and draw constants
  96 bytes. Uniform backing capacity is 256 bytes for portable CBV alignment;
  the bound ABI range remains 160 bytes.
- Helper resize is transactional. Extent-only changes retain pipelines;
  signature changes create a complete candidate family before swapping. Old
  logical handles retire through RHI submission dependencies with no idle.
- Frame tickets bind the queue head captured at prepare. Only the unique next
  published graphics token is accepted; stale/future/intermediate tokens are
  rejected. Queue progress forbids a `notSubmitted` disposition. A real submit
  after recording failure conservatively enters submitted state and cannot be
  reused until completion.
- Completion-query and teardown exceptions fail closed instead of escaping
  `noexcept`; descriptor poison rebuilds the frame table. Borrowed output and
  scene-depth resources are never destroyed.
- Multisampled scene depth is rejected because this leaf intentionally uses a
  resolved `Sampler2D<float>` contract.

